From: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Subject: crypto: acomp - enforce MAX_SYNC_COMP_REQSIZE
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:08:54 -0700

Enforce the limit MAX_SYNC_COMP_REQSIZE when an acomp tfm is
initialised.  All existing algorithms obey this limit.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20261017160918.2738626-3-usama.arif@linux.dev
Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Signed-off-by: Usama Arif <usama.arif@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: <chengming.zhou@linux.dev>
Cc: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
Cc: Johannes Weiner <hannes@cmpxchg.org>
Cc: Nhat Pham <nphamcs@gmail.com>
Cc: Nick Terrell <terrelln@fb.com>
Cc: Yosry Ahmed <yosry@kernel.org>
Cc: Rik van Riel <riel@surriel.com>
Cc: Shakeel Butt <shakeel.butt@linux.dev>
Cc: <alex@ghiti.fr>
Cc: Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
Cc: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
---

 crypto/acompress.c |   18 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/crypto/acompress.c~crypto-acomp-enforce-max_sync_comp_reqsize
+++ a/crypto/acompress.c
@@ -92,10 +92,6 @@ static int crypto_acomp_init_tfm(struct
 		if (IS_ERR(fb))
 			return PTR_ERR(fb);
 
-		err = -EINVAL;
-		if (crypto_acomp_reqsize(fb) > MAX_SYNC_COMP_REQSIZE)
-			goto out_free_fb;
-
 		tfm->fb = crypto_acomp_tfm(fb);
 	}
 
@@ -105,15 +101,19 @@ static int crypto_acomp_init_tfm(struct
 
 	acomp->base.exit = crypto_acomp_exit_tfm;
 
-	if (!alg->init)
-		return 0;
-
-	err = alg->init(acomp);
-	if (err)
+	if (alg->init && ((err = alg->init(acomp))))
 		goto out_free_fb;
 
+	err = -EINVAL;
+	if (!acomp_is_async(acomp) &&
+	    crypto_acomp_reqsize(acomp) > MAX_SYNC_COMP_REQSIZE)
+		goto out_exit_tfm;
+
 	return 0;
 
+out_exit_tfm:
+	if (alg->exit)
+		alg->exit(acomp);
 out_free_fb:
 	crypto_free_acomp(fb);
 	return err;
_
